WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.460
Hello.

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:10.480
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.760
In this tenth and final lesson,

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.700
we'll look at the various symptoms that
can come along with a mood disorder,

5
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.090
and how to cope with each.

6
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:27.720
People with bipolar disorder or bipolar spectrum
disorder often have anxiety, restlessness,

7
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:33.530
irritability, anger, and insomnia
even before their first depression.

8
00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:39.430
The first depression may improve easily,
even with a small dose of antidepressant,

9
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:45.470
but it soon returns, and over time the
response to antidepressants tends to weaken.

10
00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:51.650
Along the way, panic, drinking, self-harm, binge
eating, and poor concentration appear together,

11
00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.410
but their root is difficulty regulating mood.

12
00:00:55.630 --> 00:01:03.627
Inappropriate drug treatment that focuses only on
the visible symptoms can actually make them worse,

13
00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:07.740
so it's important to look at the mood problem as well.

14
00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:12.630
Many people have both a mood
disorder and panic disorder.

15
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:17.770
If the mood swings are not treated
first, the panic may get worse again,

16
00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:22.070
or you may be unable to stop taking tranquillisers.

17
00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:28.510
A panic attack is very distressing, but it
is not as life-threatening as it feels.

18
00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:29.590
Don't panic.

19
00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:33.930
Sit or lie down comfortably
and breathe slowly and deeply.

20
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.650
During hyperventilation,

21
00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:40.800
the feeling that you can't breathe
actually comes from breathing in too much.

22
00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.380
Don't force yourself to breathe in.

23
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:48.530
Breathe slowly, thinking of breathing
in for 5 seconds and out for 10.

24
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:52.285
Once symptoms start, it's hard to breathe slowly.

25
00:01:52.305 --> 00:01:59.190
So it's important to practise abdominal
breathing and muscle relaxation in advance.

26
00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:01.540
Depression, anxiety,

27
00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:08.040
and anger can show up as physical symptoms
such as muscle pain or indigestion.

28
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:13.730
They usually improve once your mood settles,
but relaxing the body directly also helps.

29
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:18.570
Stretching, yoga, massage, and
abdominal breathing are good.

30
00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:25.290
For tension headaches that feel like a band
squeezing your head, loosen the muscles of the head,

31
00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:29.550
neck, and shoulders with your hands or a massage tool.

32
00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.600
Difficulty controlling appetite
can be a side effect of medication,

33
00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.940
but it is also a symptom of the mood disorder itself.

34
00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:43.520
Commonly prescribed appetite suppressants can worsen

35
00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.820
mood swings and make appetite even harder to control,

36
00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:50.730
so be sure to talk with your doctor before choosing one.

37
00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:57.380
When you're depressed, you can feel urges
to harm yourself or to take your own life,

38
00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.580
because of negative thoughts about the
future, self-blame, and feeling worthless,

39
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.620
or because your emotions are unstable.

40
00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:12.080
When this happens, please come to the outpatient
clinic quickly, or come to the emergency room,

41
00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.360
and talk with the medical team.

42
00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:18.040
You can see a psychiatrist in the emergency room, too.

43
00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:24.563
In an urgent moment, you can also ask for help
at any time at the Suicide Prevention Hotline,

44
00:03:24.583 --> 00:03:27.020
109.

45
00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:32.440
Caregivers, remove dangerous items
such as sharp objects and ropes,

46
00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:36.820
and stay by their side and listen,
rather than judging or pressuring.

47
00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.480
It's important to show empathy for how hard it has been.

48
00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.780
Showing steady interest, and a stable, warm attitude,

49
00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.480
consistently is how you help
them move away from self-harm.

50
00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:55.350
During elevated periods,
irritability and anger increase,

51
00:03:55.370 --> 00:04:00.260
and you may throw things or become
violent toward people close to you.

52
00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:06.350
In everyday life, practise rating how
angry you are on a scale from 0 to 10.

53
00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:12.430
Set the point where your emotions and
behaviour are out of control at 5.

54
00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:19.270
When you reach 5 or above, don't think about
anything else; get away from the spot quickly.

55
00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.530
Anger takes about 15 seconds to peak.

56
00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:30.170
If you get through those 15 seconds well, the
emotion lessens and you can think rationally.

57
00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:35.710
When your score drops to about 2,
think calmly about why you got angry,

58
00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:39.230
and then try talking with the other person.

59
00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:47.500
Many people with a mood disorder have
attention problems similar to ADHD.

60
00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:52.940
But when mood is unstable, ADHD
medication alone has little effect,

61
00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:58.800
and if mood symptoms are mistaken
for ADHD and medication is overused,

62
00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:01.280
mood swings can actually get worse.

63
00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:06.480
First stabilise the mood, then assess
the remaining attention problems,

64
00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:10.720
and consider ADHD treatment if needed.

65
00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:16.550
It is known that repeated depressive
episodes raise the risk of dementia.

66
00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:19.830
This is thought to be because
activity and mental stimulation

67
00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:23.800
drop during depression and unhealthy habits increase.

68
00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:29.780
But if you misunderstand this as the medication
causing dementia and stop it on your own,

69
00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:33.080
the risk of dementia actually goes up.

70
00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:38.520
Taking your medication well prevents
relapse and can help your brain health too.

71
00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:46.890
Do exercise that makes you breathe hard and
sweat at least 3 times a week, and walk often.

72
00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:53.610
Avoid sweet foods and drinks, eat fish, vegetables,
fruit, and nuts, and manage your weight.

73
00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:59.280
Keep taking your diabetes, blood
pressure, and cholesterol medication too.

74
00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:04.800
See friends and relatives at least once a
month, and read aloud for 20 minutes a day.

75
00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:08.120
Quit smoking now and avoid heavy drinking.

76
00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:12.920
And take your mood disorder medication
well, because the more you relapse,

77
00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:15.790
the more the risk of dementia may rise.

78
00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:21.920
Over ten episodes, we've gone through the
contents of the Mood Disorder Guide together.

79
00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:25.900
A mood disorder is an illness that can clearly get

80
00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:29.140
better with steady treatment and lifestyle management.

81
00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.820
Please ask me anything at your visit, any time.

82
00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:36.920
The Department of Psychiatry
at Seoul National University

83
00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:41.240
Bundang Hospital sincerely supports your recovery.

84
00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.380
Thank you.
